  id: Colon
  partName: Colon
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The colon is a major part of the large intestine responsible for absorbing water
    and electrolytes from digested material. It compacts waste into feces and prepares
    it for elimination. '
  - This organ plays a key role in maintaining fluid balance and supporting digestive
    health. It also houses beneficial bacteria that aid in fermentation and nutrient
    absorption, contributing to overall gastrointestinal function and metabolic processes.
